Subject: [virtio] A Special Majority Ballot to approve Virtio v1.1 wd02 with
 Non-Material Changes made since its last public review as a Committee
 Specification has been set up
To: tc-announce@lists.oasis-open.org, members@lists.oasis-open.org, virtio@lists.oasis-open.org, virtio-comment@lists.oasis-open.org
List-ID: <virtio-comment.lists.oasis-open.org>

--0000000000000acb670585b58459
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

The VIRTIO TC members [1] have requested a Special Majority Vote to approve
Virtio v1.1 wd02  as a Committee Specification.

Changes have been made to this Committee Draft since its last public
review. The description of the changes can be inspected in the red-lined
files virtio-v1.1-wd02-diff-from-v1.1-csprd01 (highlighting changes from
v1.1-csprd01) and also virtio-v1.1-wd02-diff-from-v1.0-cs04 (highlighting
changes from v1.0-cs04) included in the specification zip package [2].

The TC judges these changes to be Non-Material in accordance with the
definition in the OASIS TC Process (
http://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process#dNonmaterialChange).
The TC requested this ballot in accordance with the procedure for approving
a Committee Specification or Note (
http://www.oasis-open.org/policies-guidelines/tc-process#Non-MaterialChangesSummary
).

The ballot can be inspected at
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/ballot.php?id=3380. The ballot opens
on 05 April 2019 and closes on 11 April 2019 at 23:59 UTC.

Any Eligible Person concerned that the changes are Material is asked to
bring their concern to OASIS TC Administration at
tc-administration@lists.oasis-open.org so that the appropriate actions can
be taken.
---

[1] OASIS Virtual I/O Device (VIRTIO) TC
https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/virtio/

[2] Working draft ZIP file package including red-lined diff files
https://github.com/oasis-tcs/virtio-docs/blob/master/virtio-v1.1-wd02.zip

